'' A NAME THAT IS BOTH A GENERIC PROCEDURE AND AN ORDINARY ONE resolves as fbc-modern does:
'' declared AFTER the ordinary overloads, the generic takes every call it is offered --
'' exact ordinary matches included, and 'H( of short )( 5 )'; declared BEFORE them, it is
'' hidden. See GenericOfSet_ in src/symbols/genericset.bas.
''
'' 'H( k )' over a MyKey -- a call only the generic can take -- was TKO0994 at the top
'' level and, inside 'Use( of K )', a MIR verifier fault, "a function returning i64
'' returns no value": the head of the chain was ordinary, so the generic was never
'' instantiated. The other calls compiled, to the ordinary overloads fbc does not choose.
''
'' A goldenrun.sh differential: built and run by fbc-modern 1.20 and by tiko, the two
'' outputs are byte-identical (measured 2026-10-10).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/generic-mixed-set.bas -o tests/driver/genericmixedset.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/genericmixedset.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/genericmixedset.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: key4040
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ordfirst30043008302430243008
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: written3002
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: genfirst1007100520041002
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
